  "notes": [
   "Each channel: Mega pin (2..13) -> blue jumper -> breadboard strip, 220 ohm resistor bridges the centre gap to the LED-anode strip, LED cathode strip is wired by a black jumper to the ground rail (tn). Exact breadboard columns are chosen for a clean layout (2 columns per channel), not copied from the image's hole positions.",
   "The ground rail tn.1..tn.12 is a single rail strip; all cathode wires and the Mega GND wire share it.",
   "The Mega GND pin (next to AREF) is assumed to be named GND.1 in the catalogue.",
   "LED anodes are the longer leg (A) on the resistor side; cathodes (C) go to ground, as in the schematic.",
   "Image pin order has pin 13 at the leftmost LED; here copy k uses pin k+1, which is electrically equivalent."
  ]
 },
